Two of the last three test runs are done and decided. The third is waiting in the queue. Nothing new was launched.

**What the two finished runs show** (document questions, 1,500 per run; score = share of answers the judge model accepts, higher is better):

| Test | Seed | Score with the change ↑ | Plain compressed score ↑ | Difference (95% range) | Share of compressed slots kept | Decision |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Ask the model to copy the evidence, then answer | 43 | .606 | .615 | −.009 [−.027, +.011] | 1.00× | Closed: no gain at either seed (seed 42 was +.001) |
| Keep only the quarter of slots the model looks at most | 43 | .619 | .615 | +.005 [−.007, +.017] | .25× (106 per question instead of 431) | Adopted: no loss at either seed (seed 42 was +.001) |

A "slot" is one compressed vector standing in for about 8 tokens of the page.

- **Main finding:** once the question is known, the model uses only about a quarter of the slots. This supports training with a question-aware slot budget. It does not save storage, because choosing the quarter needs one pass over every slot.
- **Checks passed on both runs:** no unreadable answers, all 1,500 rows present, and run on the same kind of node as their baselines.
- **One oddity:** the scheduler labels both jobs "preempted", but their last attempts finished cleanly with exit 0. I added this case to the known-issues file.

**Still running:** the test that keeps only an eighth of the slots (seed 42). It had waited 7 hours on the best-effort partition, so I let it use the regular partition too, which the campaign rules allow. Its start estimate moved from Monday to today about 13:55.

**Budget:** 64 of 65 runs used. The last one is kept to rerun a test whose output fails the checks.

**Next:** the campaign wakes when the eighth-of-slots test ends, or in 12 hours at the latest. Once it is recorded, every test in the plan is decided.

